{
  "version": 3,
  "title": "What if your plane blew up?",
  "series": "Freefall / Pick Your Landing",
  "narration": "Okay, your plane just exploded. No parachute, no warning, just a lot of sky. First your brain taps out, not enough oxygen, just blackness. Then the air starts working, and at ten thousand feet you're wide awake, holding a hundred and twenty miles an hour. Look down. A river, a forest, a rocky field, a little village, and one suspiciously beautiful plowed farm. The river is concrete wearing water. Trees might catch you if they feel charitable. Bricks are bricks. Rocks are rocks. So spread your arms, kill the spin, and steer for the farm. Five thousand feet. Two thousand. Five hundred. Feet first, knees bent, and roll. You hit the wheat, pop up, brush off your jacket, and walk away. Next time? Take the train.",
